mmap, munmap - map memory into a process

SYNOPSIS
    void *mmap(void *addr, size_t len, int prot, int flags,
               int fd, off_t offset);
    int munmap(void *addr, size_t len);

DESCRIPTION
    Pass a null address to have the kernel select a free area.
    MAP_PRIVATE maps a snapshot of a readable regular file at a
    page-aligned offset. Use PROT_READ, with PROT_WRITE for a private
    writable copy. A mapping stays valid after close and is copied
    by fork. The final partial page is zero-filled beyond the file.

    MAP_PRIVATE with MAP_ANONYMOUS, fd -1 and offset zero creates a
    zero-filled private area. Each mapping can span up to 16 MiB.
    Use munmap with the original address and length to remove it.

    MAP_SHARED is available for the framebuffer device with offset
    zero. Regular-file writeback and partial unmapping are unavailable.

RETURN VALUES
    mmap returns MAP_FAILED on error. munmap returns zero on success
    and -1 on error.

SEE ALSO
    dev(5)
